Package: ingrain
Title: Resolution-Relative Usability Audit for Occurrence Records
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Kristian", "Miok", , "kristian.miok@todo.invalid", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "ORCID_TODO"))
Description: Classifies species occurrence records into three states
    relative to a chosen analysis grain: 'inert' (positional uncertainty
    smaller than the grain, so corrections cannot act), 'usable'
    (uncertainty reported and exceeding the grain, so corrections change
    the model), and 'unreported' (no uncertainty radius given). Provides
    per-dataset summaries and visualisations for auditing 'GBIF' downloads
    before species distribution modelling.
